    "title": "Color–Magnitude Diagram (CMD)",
    "field": "Astronomy / Astrophysics",
    "plotType": "Scatter plot of magnitude vs. color index (observational HR diagram)",
    "description": "A color–magnitude diagram is the observational cousin of the HR diagram: it plots apparent (or absolute) magnitude against a color index such as B–V or G_BP–G_RP, where redder colors mean cooler stars. Applied to a star cluster — where all stars share a distance and age — the CMD shows a crisp main sequence with a turnoff point and, for older clusters, a red-giant branch and horizontal branch. It is the standard tool for dating clusters and mapping stellar populations.",
